          %h3#internal_functors Internal functors
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} Functors
            between internal categories are defined in a similar fashion. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            it is often better to use
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctors
            instead; this makes sense when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superextensive+site"} superextensive site
          %h3#alternative_definition Alternative definition
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Span
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span(A)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} spans
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Span
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span(A)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t) : C_0 \leftarrow C_1 \to C_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1 \times_{C_0} C_1
            is the vertex of the composite span
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t) \circ (s,t)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            are required to be morphisms of spans, which is equivalent to imposing the source and target axioms above. Finally the unit and associativity axioms for monads imply those above.
          %p
            This approach makes it easy to define the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+profunctor"} internal profunctor
          %h3#internal_nerve Internal nerve
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            can be generalised to give an
            %em internal nerve
            construction. For a small category,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(D)
            = succeed "-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of copies of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an internal category in some category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            required for the constructions to make sense),its nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)
            (or if more precision is needed
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{int}(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)_0 = C_0
              , the ‘object of objects’ of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)_1  = C_1
              , the ‘object of arrows’ of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)_2 = C_1 \times_{C_0} C_1
              the object of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composable+pairs"} composable pairs
              of arrows of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 3
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(C)_3 = C_1 \times_{C_0} C_1\times_{C_0} C_1
              , the object of composable triples of arrows;
          %p
            and so on. Face and degeneracy morphisms are induced from the structural moprhisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            in a fairly obvious way.
          %p Internal functors between internal categories induce simplicial morphisms between the corresponding nerves.
          %h3#internal_category_in_homotopy_type_theory Internal category in homotopy type theory
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+homotopy+type+theory"} internal category in homotopy type theory
          %h3#higher_internal_categories Higher internal categories
          %p
            One can also look at this in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and consider internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+category"} n-fold category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+infinity-groupoid"} internal infinity-groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} internal (infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28infinity%2Cn%29-category"} internal (infinity,n)-category
          %p
            The general concept is that of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-by-k+category"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n \times k)
                \-category
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            is a category internal to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            is a set of objects and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            is a set of morphisms and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
          %p
            Historically, the motivating example was (apparently) the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            internal to the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                smooth category
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/smooth+category"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
            is a groupoid internal to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+concrete+category"} topological concrete category
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strictly
            and the collection of objects is small.) In these examples,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            is a “space of objects” and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            a “space of morphisms”.
          %p Further examples:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A category internal to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %li
              %p
                A groupoid internal to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+sets"} definable sets
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+groupoid"} definable groupoid
            %li
              %p
                A groupoid internal to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+of+groupoids"} presheaf of groupoids
            %li
              %p
                A groupoid internal to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+Hopf+algebroid"} commutative Hopf algebroid
            %li
              %p
                A pointed one-object category internal to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
            %li
              %p
                A pointed one-object groupoid internal to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-group"} H-group
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocategory"} cocategory
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a category internal to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
                is a category internal to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+bicategory"} double bicategory
                is a category internal to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bicat"} Bicat
                (in a suitably weak sense).
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                is equivalent to a category internal to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
            %li
              %p
                A
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Baez-Crans 2-vector space
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Baez-Crans+2-vector+space"} ?
                is a category internal to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
                is an internal category in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                and so has an internal nerve, which is a simplicial object in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi δ
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C\stackrel{\delta}{\to}P)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi δ
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C\stackrel{\delta}{\to}P)
                has
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                having
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                in dimension 0, and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                in dimension 1, with the trivial group in all other dimensions. The only possible non-trivial boundary map from dimension 1 to dimension 0 is then the boundary
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                of the crossed module.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#CartesianClosure In a cartesian closed category
          %p
            If the ambient (finitely complete) category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat(\mathbf{E})
            of categories internal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
            is also cartesian closed. This was
            %a{:href => "#BastianiEhresmann_69"} proved
            %a{:href => "#BastianiEhresmann_72"} twice
            by
