          %p
            For the precise statement see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "2-topos#InTermsOfInternalCategories"} 2-topos – In terms of internal categories
          %h2#internalization_versus_enrichment Internalization versus enrichment
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization+versus+enrichment"} internalization versus enrichment
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+internal+category"} locally internal category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"}> indexed category
                ,
                %span.newWikiWord
                  externalisation
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/externalisation"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+a+monoidal+category"} internal category in a monoidal category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence+of+internal+categories"} weak equivalence of internal categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} category object in an (infinity,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "2-topos#InTermsOfInternalCategories"} 2-Topos – In terms of internal categories
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-congruence"} 2-congruence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n+%C3%97+k%29-category"} (n × k)-category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+site"} internal site
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %h2#References References
          %p The general definition of internal categories seems to have first been formulated in:
          %ul
            %li#Grothendieck61
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              , p. 106 (9 of 21) of:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
              = succeed "," do
                %em Techniques de construction et théorèmes d’existence en géométrie algébrique III: préschémas quotients
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1960-1961__6__99_0"} numdam:SB_1960-1961__6__99_0
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/SB_1960-1961__6__99_0.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://translations.thosgood.com/fga/fga3.iii.xml"} web version
          %p
            following the general principle of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            formulated in
          %ul
            %li#Grothendieck60
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              , p. 370 (3 of 23) in:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
              = succeed "," do
                %em Technique de descente et théorèmes d’existence en géométrie algébriques. II: Le théorème d’existence en théorie formelle des modules
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/SB_1958-1960__5__369_0"} numdam:SB_1958-1960__5__369_0
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/SB_1958-1960__5__369_0.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://translations.thosgood.com/fga/fga3.ii.xml"} web version
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoids"} topological groupoids
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégories topologiques et categories différentiables
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EhresmannCategoriesTopologiques.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an:0205.28202"} zbMath:0205.28202
          %p
            and their understanding as categories internal to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TopologicalSpaces"} TopologicalSpaces
            and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothManifolds"} SmoothManifolds
            is often attributed to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégories structurées
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/ASENS_1963_3_80_4_349_0"} numdam:ASENS_1963_3_80_4_349_0
          %p
            but it seems that the definition is not actually contained in there, certainly not in its simple and widely understood form due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Grothendieck61"} Grothendieck 61
          %p
            The observation that (internal) categories are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+spans"} bicategory of spans
          %ul
            %li#Bunge66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories of set valued functors
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Bunge-CategoriesOfSetValuedFunctors.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li{:id => "Bénabou67"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
                , §5.4.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Bicategories
                %strong 47
                Springer (1967) 1-77 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0074299"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0074299
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Celeyrette"}> Jean Celeyrette
                ,
                %em Catégories internes et fibrations
                \&amp;
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomologie de Gel’fand-Fuks
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/files/celeyrette-thesis-1975.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaves"}> 2-sheaves
            ) as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences+of+internal+categories"} weak equivalences of internal categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"} Robert Paré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stacks and equivalence of indexed categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers de Top. et Géom. Diff. Catég
                %strong 20
                4 (1979) 373-399 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1979__20_4_373_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1979__20_4_373_0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stack completions and Morita equivalence for categories in a topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers de Top. et Géom. Diff. Catég
                %strong 20
                4, (1979) 401-436 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1979__20_4_401_0"}> numdam
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=558106"} MR558106
          %p
            Establishing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+Cat"} canonical model structure
            for internal categories in a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
              = succeed "," do
                %em Strong stacks and classifying spaces
              %em Category Theory
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Como"}> Como
              , 1990), Lecture Notes in Mathematics
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1488
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0084222"} doi:10.1007/BFb0084222
          %p
            and in the further generality of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+categories"} finitely complete categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomas+Everaert"}> Tomas Everaert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudger+W.+Kieboom"} Rudger W. Kieboom
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Van+der+Linden"} Tim Van der Linden
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model structures for homotopy of internal categories
              %strong 15
              3 (CT2004) 66-94 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/15/3/15-03abs.html"}> tac:15-03
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review of the basics of internal categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magnus+Forrester-Barker"}> Magnus Forrester-Barker
              ,
              %em Group Objects and Internal Categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212065"}> arXiv:math/0212065
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+profunctors"} internal profunctors
            between internal categories (without recalling their definition) is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Benabou73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              , §5.1 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Les distributeurs
              %strong 33
              (1973) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.entretemps.asso.fr/maths/DistributeursLouvain.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Benabou-LesDistributeurs.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An early textbook account with explicit definitions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functors"} internal functors
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+profunctors"} internal profunctors
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              , Chapter 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topos theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 10
          %p Further textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §XII.1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (second ed. 1997) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Chapter 8 in Vol 1,
                %em Basic Category Theory
                , of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525858"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525858
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
                , Chapter 7 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical Logic and Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 141
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/studies-in-logic-and-the-foundations-of-mathematics/vol/141"} ISBN:978-0-444-50170-7
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.mpi-sws.org/~dreyer/courses/catlogic/jacobs.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and with emphasis on an ambient
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , Section B2.3 in: Vol. 1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant+--+A+Topos+Theory+Compendium"} Sketches of an Elephant – A Topos Theory Compendium
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/sketches-of-an-elephant-9780198534259"} ISBN:9780198534259
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
                (1992)
          %p
            Survey and introduction with an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Pradines"}> Jean Pradines
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    In
                    = succeed "\u2018s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann"} Ehresmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.1608"} arXiv:0711.1608
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.impan.pl/en/publishing-house/banach-center-publications/all/76/0/86184/in-ehresmann-s-footsteps-from-group-geometries-to-groupoid-geometries"} doi:10.4064/bc76-0-5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alissa+Crans"} Alissa Crans
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307263"} Higher-Dimensional Algebra VI: Lie 2-Algebras
          %p
            The original proofs that the category of internal categories is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            when the ambient category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} finitely complete
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            are in
          %ul
            %li#BastianiEhresmann_69
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9e+Bastiani"}> Andrée Bastiani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"} Charles Ehresmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories de foncteurs structurés
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1969__11_3_329_0"} numdam:CTGDC_1969__11_3_329_0
            %li#BastianiEhresmann_72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9e+Bastiani"}> Andrée Bastiani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"} Charles Ehresmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories of sketched structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1972__13_2_104_0"} Numdam
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+Ghiorzi"}> Enrico Ghiorzi
              , Section 1.2 of:
              %em Complete internal categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.08741"}> arXiv:2004.08741
              )
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spans"} spans
          %ul
            %li
              Renato Betti,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Formal theory of internal categories
              %a{:href => "http://www.dmi.unict.it/ojs/index.php/lematematiche/article/view/456/427"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure"} canonical model structure
            on categories of internal categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomas+Everaert"}> Tomas Everaert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudger+W.+Kieboom"} Rudger W. Kieboom
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Van+der+Linden"} Tim Van der Linden
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model structures for homotopy of internal categories
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/15/3/15-03abs.html"} tac:15-03
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            between internal categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"}> David Roberts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Internal categories, anafunctors and localisations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theory+and+Applications+of+Categories"} Theory and Applications of Categories
              %strong 26
              29 (2012) 29 788-829 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/29/26-29abs.html"}> tac:26-29
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1101.2363"} arXiv:1101.2363
          %p
            An old discussion on variants of internal categories, crossed modules and 2-groups is archived
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://nforum.mathforge.org/discussion/621/internal-category/?Focus=29967#Comment_29967"} here
          %p A good general reference:
          %ul
            %li
              Adrian Miranda:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Internal categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://figshare.mq.edu.au/articles/thesis/Internal_categories/19434626"} url
              = succeed "&rbrack;," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Miranda-InternalCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
        .revisedby
